    <script type="application/ld+json">{"mainEntity":{"headline":"Determinants of groundwater accessibility to the rural community in the coastal area of the Indian Sundarban","description":"Groundwater accessibility is a challenging issue in the coastal area of the Indian Sundarban. The study focuses on assessing the groundwater accessibility, considering groundwater quality, availability and people’s perception of its access. Four dimensions (social, demographic, economic and physical), covering twenty-seven variables, have been considered to assess groundwater accessibility. A structured questionnaire was used to assess the social, demographic, economic and physical dimensions of groundwater accessibility at household level. Groundwater samples (324) collected during the pre- and post-monsoon seasons in 2023, 2024 and 2025 were analysed for physicochemical properties. Pearson’s correlation matrix and linear regression were used to show the relationships among groundwater parameters and socio-demographic variables respectively. The results show a strong positive relationship among groundwater parameters such as electrical conductivity (EC), total dissolved solids (TDS), chloride (Cl) and total hardness (TH), which are found in high concentrations near rivers, creeks, and the coast. An inverse relationship has been observed between the amount of water and the distance required for water collection. Carrying water over long distances is a particular challenge, especially for women (58.73%) and adolescent girls (44.44%). 51.89% of the households located within 1 km of the river/creek/coast can obtain water within 15–30 min. The findings indicate that groundwater accessibility is constrained by factors related to availability, access and quality. Zone-wise analysis of these complex challenges in water accessibility can help to develop specific management plans to achieve Sustainable Development Goal (SDG 6).","datePublished":"2026-09-28T00:00:00Z","dateModified":"2026-09-28T00:00:00Z","pageStart":"1","pageEnd":"33","sameAs":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10668-026-08152-0","keywords":["Groundwater use","Water quality","Rural community","Coastal region","Sustainable management","Sustainable Development","Environmental Management","Environmental Economics","Ecology","Economic Growth","Economic Geology"],"image":["https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10668-026-08152-0/MediaObjects/10668_2026_8152_Figa_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10668-026-08152-0/MediaObjects/10668_2026_8152_Fig1_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10668-026-08152-0/MediaObjects/10668_2026_8152_Fig2_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10668-026-08152-0/MediaObjects/10668_2026_8152_Fig3_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10668-026-08152-0/MediaObjects/10668_2026_8152_Fig4_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10668-026-08152-0/MediaObjects/10668_2026_8152_Fig5_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10668-026-08152-0/MediaObjects/10668_2026_8152_Fig6_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10668-026-08152-0/MediaObjects/10668_2026_8152_Fig7_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10668-026-08152-0/MediaObjects/10668_2026_8152_Fig8_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10668-026-08152-0/MediaObjects/10668_2026_8152_Fig9_HTML.png"],"isPartOf":{"name":"Environment, Development and Sustainability","issn":["1573-2975"],"@type":["Periodical"]},"publisher":{"name":"Springer Netherlands","logo":{"url":"https://www.springernature.com/app-sn/public/images/logo-springernature.png","@type":"ImageObject"},"@type":"Organization"},"author":[{"name":"Monali Biswas","url":"http://orcid.org/0009-0003-2280-996X","affiliation":[{"name":"Diamond Harbour Women’s University","address":{"name":"Department of Geography, Diamond Harbour Women’s University, Sarisha, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"email":"monalipiubiswas@gmail.com","@type":"Person"},{"name":"Sujit Mandal","affiliation":[{"name":"Diamond Harbour Women’s University","address":{"name":"Department of Geography, Diamond Harbour Women’s University, Sarisha, India","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"}],"isAccessibleForFree":false,"hasPart":{"isAccessibleForFree":false,"cssSelector":".main-content","@type":"WebPageElement"},"@type":"ScholarlyArticle"},"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage"}</script>

        
        
